# Copy to .env and fill in what you need. `.env` is loaded automatically by
# `slopsaver` and by the sandbox chaos scripts (see slopsaver/__main__.py and
# sandbox/chaos/_common.py) — nothing else needs to source this file.
#
# Real shell/CI env vars always take precedence over .env; this file is a
# convenience for local dev, not a secrets store — never commit .env itself.

# --- Reasoning agent (required unless you always run with --fake-reasoner) ---
# The Claude Agent SDK resolves credentials in this order: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
# then ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, then an `ant auth login` profile. If you've
# already run `ant auth login`, you can leave this unset.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# --- Stripe adapter (config/customer.example.yaml -> integrations.stripe) ---
# A restricted, read-only key is enough unless you enable webhook replay.
STRIPE_API_KEY=

# --- S3 / MinIO adapter ---
# For the kind sandbox, these match sandbox/k8s/all.yaml's MinIO deployment.
# For real AWS, use an IAM key scoped to the one bucket.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=slopsaver
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=slopsaver123

# --- Self-monitoring heartbeat (optional) ---
# Only needed if config/customer.yaml sets `heartbeat_url` to a private URL
# you'd rather not hardcode. Most Healthchecks.io-style URLs are fine inline.
# HEARTBEAT_URL=
